  "zero_semantics": "Go: a zero value means the default, for every option, because a struct cannot tell unset from zero. Node: undefined means the default; an explicit 0 is a value where it is legal (max_age: a background refresh whenever the gate is open; min_refresh_interval: no failure gate) and an error where it is not (max_bytes, max_stale, timeout).",
